-- title:
--   Galois descent of automorphisms along a constant-field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, and let $\iota_A : L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be a ring homomorphism into the algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$. For a field $K$ of characteristic zero write $K \cdot F$ for `laurentBaseChange K F`, the intermediate field of $K((q))$ over $K$ generated by the image of $F$ under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to K((q))$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to K$; for $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, `arithmeticGalois F τ` is the element of the group of pairs $(\text{ring automorphism of } \overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F, \text{ring automorphism of } \overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ compatible with the structure map whose first component acts coefficientwise by $\tau$ and whose second component is $\tau$. Let $\theta$ be a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \cdot F$ commuting with the action of `arithmeticGalois F τ` for every $\tau$ fixing $\iota_A(x)$ for all $x \in L$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an $L$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $L \cdot F$ such that for all $f \in L \cdot F$ and $g \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \cdot F$ whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of that of $f$ under $\iota_A$, the underlying series of $\theta(g)$ is the coefficientwise image of that of $\sigma(f)$.
--
--   This is Galois descent for automorphisms of a constant-field extension of a function field presented through $q$-expansions: an automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \cdot F$ commuting with $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\iota_A(L))$ descends to the $L$-form $L \cdot F$. It is used in the study of the Néron model of $J_H$ at $p$, where automorphisms of modular function fields given over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ must be realised over a smaller coefficient field in order to compare idempotents, pairings and toric components.
